HONEST READING: fixed-tau clip and AdaGrad-Norm are BOUNDED-step methods, so they do
NOT diverge like OGD/scale-dependent clipping -- they belong in Table 1's stable group,
and are accuracy-competitive with (fixed-tau per-step: better than) SN-OMD. SN-OMD is
thus one of SEVERAL scale-free bounded methods here; its edge is the predictable tracker
+ dynamic-regret analysis, not a Jane accuracy win. This supports the review's C2.
